ner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-06T18:52:46Z","updated_at":"2024-01-07T00:03:18Z","body":"I ran into this issue on Debian 12 and Gitea 1.21.3 after a clean install. Installing from binary, following the docs. I found that if app.ini does not exist, then the issue occurs, i.e. the service status stays stuck on \"activating\". Attached are the results of `systemctl status gitea` and the relevant contents of gitea.service.\r\n\r\nHowever, once app.ini exists with the correct permissions, the gitea service works normally. (So I can get around the issue by running gitea manually, completing the web setup, then stopping gitea and launching it as a service at that point.)\r\n\r\nWhen I delete app.ini, the problem returns, and when I put app.ini back, the problem disappears.\r\n\r\n[systemctl_status_gitea.txt](https://github.com/go-gitea/gitea/files/13850856/systemctl_status_gitea.txt)\r\n[gitea_service.txt](https://github.com/go-gitea/gitea/files/13850857/gitea_service.txt)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-gitea/gitea/issues/comments/1879782321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bowaggoner","id":11153058,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTUzMDU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11153058?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner","html_url":"https://github.com/bowaggoner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bowaggoner/following{